<Doc
  title="Privacy Policy · THRUSTLINE"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="What THRUSTLINE stores, why, who handles it and how to delete it. No accounts, no ads, no analytics, no tracking."
  updated="22 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    THRUSTLINE is a free, open-source multiplayer game. There are no accounts, no ads, no analytics and no
    tracking. This page lists everything the game keeps, why it keeps it and how to remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>What the game stores</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A random player ID.</strong> Created the first time you play, so the server can tell players apart. It is not linked to your name, email address, phone number or Google account.</li>
    <li><strong>Your callsign.</strong> The name you choose, or a random one. Other players see it in matches and on the season board.</li>
    <li><strong>Your progress.</strong> XP and level, kills, deaths, wins, rounds played, best kills in a round, season points and when you last played. Other players can see this.</li>
    <li><strong>Match data.</strong> Your position, health, score, team and connection ping while you are in a room. It is deleted when you leave the room.</li>
    <li><strong>A transfer key.</strong> A random secret that lets your progress move with you if the game changes servers. Only the server and your device know it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The game does not ask for or collect your real name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos, location or payment details.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Your login token, transfer key, settings and volume levels are saved in the browser storage for the game's
    site. In the Android app this is Chrome's storage for the same site, so the app and Chrome on one phone share
    the same progress.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Its fonts, images and videos are served from the site
    itself, so visiting it sends no requests to other companies.
  </p>

  <h2>The Android app</h2>
  <p>
    The app opens the game's website in Chrome, or in Android's built-in WebView if Chrome is missing. It asks
    only for internet access and for permission to check whether you are online, so it can show an offline
    screen. It collects nothing of its own and has no advertising ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Who handles the data</h2>
  <p>Three providers host THRUSTLINE and process data only to deliver it:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>SpacetimeDB Maincloud</strong>, run by Clockwork Labs, hosts the game server and the data listed above.</li>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts the game's website.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Like any web service, they receive your IP address and basic request details in order to answer your device,
    and may keep short technical logs. The game server also logs when a player connects. Nothing is sold, and
    nothing is shared with anyone for advertising or any other purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Match data is deleted as soon as you leave a room.</li>
    <li>The season board starts fresh every month.</li>
    <li>Your profile stays until you ask for it to be deleted, so your level is there when you come back.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Clearing the game site's data in your browser removes your ID from your device and starts you over. In the
    Android app, long-press the THRUSTLINE icon, open <em>Site settings</em> and clear the stored data.
  </p>
  <p>
    To have your profile removed from the server too, <a href={ISSUES_URL}>open an issue on GitHub</a> with your
    callsign and level, and it will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    All traffic between your device and THRUSTLINE is encrypted (HTTPS and secure WebSockets). The server checks
    every move and hit, so other players cannot change your score or progress.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>THRUSTLINE is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from them.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date. The full history of
    this page is public in the project's repository.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy are welcome on <a href={ISSUES_URL}>GitHub</a>.</p>
</Doc>
